OL,3,GNEWSAI bought a generator following
OL,4,Agovernment's disaster warning, says dad
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man has told how he decided to buy a
OL,7,Fpower generator following the
OL,8,Fgovernment's warning to prepare for a
OL,9,Fnational emergency - to help protect
OL,10,Fhis business and also his neighbours.
OL,12,FBarry Wong spent about #550 on the
OL,13,Fappliance for his cleaning business,
OL,14,Fbut also hopes it will help him look
OL,15,Fafter his family and elderly neighbours
OL,16,Fif the power ever goes off.
OL,18,FThe 53-year-old from Prenton, Wirral,
OL,19,Fsaid the government's recent Be Ready
OL,20,Fcampaign had made him think more about
OL,21,Fhow he would cope without electricity.
OL,23,APub: 16-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
